{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>כבוד, שמים, הגו, הגו</b> — four joined [by the letter bet through he]. And likewise the interpretation: the glory of Elohim — a matter of His glory in the recounting of His created deeds. He hid it from nothingness, for who can recount His glory and reach His limit? And it is not to wonder at if we find 'declare His glory among the nations' (הגידו בגוים את כבודו) and 'tell His glory among the peoples' (והגידו את כבודו בעמים), for this verse speaks of the destruction of enemies and the deliverance of friends." "<b>וכבוד מלכים</b> — that which is glory to them is to investigate a matter, and do not investigate the deed of Elohim, for the heavens are above man and man is far below them, and the kings who have the ability to engage in wisdom alone — there is no searching. And the reason: they cannot investigate His glory and know what is above and what is below, though you may search it out. As when the refiner removes and smelts away the dross of silver, then from the refiner a vessel comes out as he desires, so too the king removes the wicked who is before him, and then his throne is established in righteousness — and this is their glory and their splendor, to investigate in judgment, until they are meticulous in the laws of kingship."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Reading 'מאין' as 'מן אין' (from nothingness); text is elliptical and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:39.482520318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}